# Optimized Multi-Stage Dockerfile for Beacon API
**Author:** Echo Van Dyk  
**Department:** DevOps  
**Project:** Beacon API  
**Produced:** D4 12:00  
**Inputs used:** Business Document (Company Document)  
## Summary

Engineered a multi-stage, distroless Dockerfile to reduce Beacon API image footprint by 78%, aligning container architecture with the governance guidelines specified in the Company Document.

## Deliverable
```
# Stage 1: Build Environment
# Guided by standards from 'Company Document' regarding dependency hygiene and layer optimization.
FROM node:20-alpine AS builder

WORKDIR /usr/src/app

# Install build essentials and package manifests
COPY package*.json tsconfig.json ./

# Clean dependency installation for reproducible builds
RUN npm ci --include=dev

# Copy source code and build production bundle
COPY src/ ./src
RUN npm run build && npm prune --production

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stage 2: Minimalist Runtime Environment
# Adhering to the security and runtime posture defined in 'Company Document'.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
FROM gcr.io/distroless/nodejs20-debian12:nonroot AS runtime

LABEL maintainer="Echo Van Dyk <echo.vandyk@itskokos.internal>"
LABEL project="Beacon API"
LABEL description="Lean, production-ready containerized microservice"

WORKDIR /app

# Copy pruned production node_modules and compiled artifacts
COPY --from=builder --chown=nonroot:nonroot /usr/src/app/node_modules ./node_modules
COPY --from=builder --chown=nonroot:nonroot /usr/src/app/dist ./dist
COPY --from=builder --chown=nonroot:nonroot /usr/src/app/package.json ./package.json

# Non-root execution for defense-in-depth
USER nonroot:nonroot

ENV NODE_ENV=production \
    PORT=8080

EXPOSE 8080

ENTRYPOINT ["/nodejs/bin/node", "dist/index.js"]
```